{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T05:46:45.361811+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE1_BASELINE", "phase": "PHASE_1_THREE_AGENT_MAJORITY_BASELINE", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "OFFLINE", "monitor_ai": "OFFLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "OFFLINE", "event": "GATEKEEPER_RESPONSE", "direction": "INBOUND_FROM_GATEKEEPER", "thread_id": "tx_phase1_baseline_6eedd4bf", "turn": 2, "legacy_status": "REJECTED", "gatekeeper_status": "SOFT_REJECT", "gatekeeper_turn": 2, "frustration_score": null, "reply_text": "Not enough detail. \"Standardized DD\" is vague\u2014every vendor claims speed.\n\n**Before scheduling:** \n\n1. What % of our deal flow actually fits your standardized model vs. bespoke asks?\n2. How do you handle edge cases (regulatory complexity, sector-specific risks)?\n3. What's your actual error rate on first-pass reports?\n\nA 15-min call only makes sense if you can show your overflow work actually reduces *our analysts' rework cycles*\u2014not just shifts grunt work. \n\nSend a one-pager with concrete metrics: turnaround proof, rework stats, pipeline fit assumptions. Then we talk."}
